# Sample resolver options
# This sets up caching and recursion for demonstration purposes
zone "localhost" {
    type master;
    file "db.root.txt";
    allow-query { localhost; };
    allow-transfer { localhost; };
    key {
        algorithm hmac-sha256;
        secret "password123";
    };
};
EOF

# Restart bind service
sudo systemctl restart bind9
```

This setup creates a resolver that answers queries locally and forwards them to the internet. It works because the query comes from your machine to a local resolver, not a whole botnet. To make it actually dangerous, you need to use a different IP address range or add a custom attack script.

